#: ../../../get_started/targets.md:150
msgid "Creating targets programmatically"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started/targets.md:152
msgid ""
"TileLang exposes the helper `tilelang.backend.target.determine_target` "
"(returns a canonical target string or config by default, or the `Target` "
"object when `return_object=True`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started/targets.md:155
msgid ""
"from tilelang.backend.target import determine_target\n"
"\n"
"tvm_target = determine_target(\n"
"    {\"kind\": \"cuda\", \"arch\": \"sm_100f\", \"code\": [\"sm_100a\", "
"\"sm_103a\"]},\n"
"    return_object=True,\n"
")\n"
"kernel = tilelang.compile(func, target=tvm_target)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started/targets.md:165
msgid "You can also build targets directly through TVM:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started/targets.md:167
msgid ""
"from tvm.target import Target\n"
"\n"
"target = Target(\"cuda\", host=\"llvm\")\n"
"target = target.with_host(Target({\"kind\": \"llvm\", \"mcpu\": "
"\"skylake\"}))\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started/targets.md:174
msgid ""
"TileLang accepts bare target strings, target config dictionaries, and "
"`Target` inputs. For targets with options, prefer config dictionaries over "
"CLI-style strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started/targets.md:177
msgid "Troubleshooting tips"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started/targets.md:179
msgid ""
"If you see `Target {'kind': 'cuda', 'arch': 'sm_80'} is not supported`, "
"double-check the spellings and that the option is valid for the target kind. "
"Any invalid option will surface as a target-construction error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started/targets.md:181
msgid ""
"If CUDA `code` fails validation, make sure it is a list of exact SM code "
"tokens, for example `[\"sm_100a\", \"sm_103a\"]`, not a comma-separated "
"string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started/targets.md:183
msgid ""
"Runtime errors such as “no kernel image is available” usually mean the "
"`arch` value does not match the GPU you are running on. Try dropping the "
"flag or switching to the correct compute capability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../get_started/targets.md:185
msgid ""
"When targeting multiple environments, use `auto` for convenience and "
"override with an explicit config only when you need architecture-specific "
"tuning."
msgstr ""
